follow14cleanRef2.prompt:
Create ONE production-ready pixel-art overworld walking sprite sheet for the SAME Gaon リーフォード shown in reference images. The references are the approved front and rear character designs, NOT sheet layouts. Preserve this exact species' anatomy, distinctive silhouette, colors, markings, clothing, accessories, face, ears, horns, tail and number of limbs. Do not redesign into a different animal. Make natural body-part animation, never just paste, stretch, shift or rotate the same static pose.
Output EXACTLY 8 separate complete sprites in a STRICT 4-column by 2-row grid of equal cells, with clear transparent gutters. Landscape 2:1 canvas preferred. Every cell contains this ONE creature only at identical scale, centered on the same local anchor. No text, no labels, no grid lines, no shadows, no ground, no effects outside sprite, no checkered backdrop. Genuinely transparent alpha background.
Columns in BOTH rows, left to right:
1 = FRONT facing DOWN toward viewer, face visible;
2 = BACK facing UP away from viewer, rear body visible, no front face;
3 = RIGHT side profile facing screen RIGHT, nose/head toward right;
4 = LEFT side profile facing screen LEFT, nose/head toward left.
Row 1 = movement pose A; Row 2 = complementary movement pose B.
Two-frame walking cycle: pose A advances left leg(s) and withdraws right leg(s); pose B advances right leg(s) and withdraws left. Existing arms and tail counter-swing naturally. Quadrupeds use alternating diagonal leg pairs; bipeds use two legs. Keep reference anatomy.
Use a slightly elevated orthographic RPG map view, crisp square pixel clusters, dark readable outlines, clean limited palette shading matching reference. At least 12% padding within every cell, entire feet/wings/horns/tail visible. Consistent head/body size and baseline across all 8 frames. Both pose frames in each facing must clearly differ through natural movement of the creature's existing limbs/wings/fins/tail. Do not add nonexistent limbs.

